From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump hono 4.13.13 -> 4.13.16 and papaparse 5.5.3 -> 5.7.1

Upstream: https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16
Upstream: https://github.com/mholt/PapaParse/releases/tag/5.7.1

Hono before 4.13.16 is affected by CVE-2026-126355, CVE-2026-126356,
CVE-2026-126357, CVE-2026-126358 and CVE-2026-126359 (csrf() ping
bypass, validator('form') Content-Type bypass, mount() path forwarding,
RegExpRouter wildcard middleware omission, css helper tag sanitization).
PapaParse before 5.7.1 is affected by CVE-2026-127056 (quadratic
parsing of delimiter-free quoted CSV input). The papaparse pin appears
in both the root package.json and packages/grafana-data/package.json.
Yarn cache regenerated and uploaded to lookaside.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -218,7 +218,7 @@
     "nx": "22.5.4",
     "open": "^10.2.0",
     "ora": "^9.0.0",
-    "papaparse": "5.5.3",
+    "papaparse": "5.7.1",
     "pdf-parse": "^1.1.1",
     "postcss": "8.5.23",
     "postcss-loader": "8.1.1",
@@ -450,7 +450,8 @@
     "body-parser@npm:^2.2.1": "2.4.0",
     "follow-redirects": "1.16.2",
     "joi@npm:^17.11.0": "17.13.9",
-    "joi@npm:^18.2.1": "18.3.1"
+    "joi@npm:^18.2.1": "18.3.1",
+    "hono": "4.13.16"
